# The calculator is a single static HTML file — it does not read env vars at runtime.
#
# The email-capture form POSTs to /api/capture (a generic endpoint name).
# If you deploy this behind a backend (Vercel/Netlify function, Express, etc.)
# that forwards captured leads to Brevo / Sendgrid / Mailchimp / etc.,
# set the provider keys there. Example:
#
# BREVO_API_KEY=
# MAILCHIMP_API_KEY=
# MAILCHIMP_LIST_ID=
